## Direction A — **Cloth Index** (recommended)
`design/a-1-page.png` · `design/a-2-transition.png` · `design/a-3-mobile.png`

Cloth first, at a scale you can't buy from, then a scroll-scrubbed weave dissolve resolves it into an **authored technical drawing** of that exact garment — and that same drawing FLIPs into its tile in the shop index. The motion device and the buy view are the same object, so it stays coherent across all nine garments instead of being a hero trick. Paper/ink/thread-red, Bodoni Moda display against IBM Plex Mono spec type. I drew and inspected all nine flats (`design/_work/flatsheet.png`), each to its own detail sentence — corozo front and patch pockets on the chore jacket, the single forward pleat, the shawl collar, the 7in inseam.

## Direction B — **The Rail**
`design/b-1-page.png` · `design/b-2-transition.png` · `design/b-3-mobile.png`

Cinematic: black/bone/signal-orange, Anton at 200px, one hard duotone unifying all photography, and a pinned scene where vertical scroll drives a garment rail sideways across three depth layers while the centred garment **de-pixelates** as it arrives, then scales into the buy panel.

## The finding that separates them
There is **no callable image generator in this session** — no host tool, no local runtime, no credentials; `dreative preflight` confirms `image-generation: permitted-but-tool-unverified`, substitutes "sourced image / procedural graphic". Details and probes in `design-blocker.md`. Keyless sourcing (Openverse, Wikimedia) works and gives excellent *cloth macros*, but cannot give a coherent nine-garment studio set for a fictional label — the contact sheets in `design/_work/` show why.

So: the mockups are browser-rendered compositions from real assets, not diffusion images, and that is named. Direction A makes the constraint the concept (cloth is real, the drawing admits it's a drawing, and the buy view is the most accurate thing on the page). Direction B inherits it — its hero images are representative and visibly not the described garments, which I've labelled on the page and called out in its plan. If you supply garment imagery or add a generator, B gets materially stronger and I'd revisit it.

Both plans cover the full route through the ending — filter with counts, size selection with sold-out states, bag with subtotal and the free-delivery gap, the complete size chart, care, shipping, reviews, shop facts — plus mobile reflow and a separate reduced-motion form.

